                "title": "Adding fractions",
                "text": "To add fractions, you must find a common denominator. The common denominator for $$\\frac{1}{2}$$ and $$\\frac{1}{3}$$ is $$6$$ since the least common multiple of $$2$$ and $$3$$ is $$6$$.",
                "variabilization": {},
                "oer": "",
                "license": ""
            },
            {
                "id": "aeba74cA222-lawsexpsamebase-P05a-h2-s2",
                "type": "hint",
                "dependencies": [],
                "title": "Adding fractions",
                "text": "We find \\n $$\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{2}{6}=\\frac{2+3}{6}=\\frac{5}{6}$$.",
